# Unity Architecture & Coding Standards

See [PROJECT_INDEX.txt](mdc:Assets/ProjectFiles/PROJECT_INDEX.txt) for complete system overview.

## Core Systems

- **Networking**: Netcode for GameObjects, Unity Transport, Unity Relay, Unity Lobby
- **Movement**: CharacterController-based (Starter Assets FirstPersonController)
- **Input**: Unity New Input System
- **Camera**: Cinemachine
- **Rendering**: URP (Universal Render Pipeline)

## Architecture Rules

- CharacterController-based movement (not Rigidbody locomotion)
- Owner-authoritative movement for network players
- GameState system with Bootstrap scene persistence
- Scene flow: Boot → MainMenu → Lobby → LoadingGame → Gameplay
- Consult latest STATE_vX file in [Assets/ProjectFiles](mdc:Assets/ProjectFiles) before architectural changes
- Systems defined in STATE_vX are assumed implemented and working

## Coding Standards

- Clean Unity C# code
- No magic numbers (use serialized fields or constants)
- No unnecessary complexity
- Clear separation of responsibility (e.g., Receiver vs Ability vs Controller)
- All physics interactions must function with CharacterController
- Avoid Rigidbody unless explicitly required
- Never suggest editing package files directly
- Always prefer scalable architecture over hacks

## Player Roles

- **Runner**: Moves on elevated obstacle course, respawns on fall
- **Sabotager**: Moves on ground, uses abilities to disrupt runners
- Supports up to 4 Runners and 4 Sabotagers

## Key Script Locations

- GameState: [GameStateController](mdc:Assets/Scripts), [SceneLoader](mdc:Assets/Scripts)
- Networking: [RelayLobbyNetwork](mdc:Assets/Scripts), [UGSBootstrap](mdc:Assets/Scripts)
- Gameplay: [GameModeManager](mdc:Assets/Scripts/Gameplay/GameModes), [PlayerRole](mdc:Assets/Scripts)
- Abilities: [TargetedPushAbility](mdc:Assets/Scripts)
- Knockback: [KnockbackReceiver](mdc:Assets/Scripts), [KnockbackMovementAdapter](mdc:Assets/Scripts)
